{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat site/index.html site/app.js'","aggregated_output":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Field notes</title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index,follow\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n<header><a href=\"/\">Field notes</a></header>\n<main id=\"app\"><p class=\"loading\">Loading…</p></main>\n<script src=\"/app.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n// Renders the home list or one note, depending on the path.\n(async function () {\n  const app = document.getElementById(\"app\");\n  const m = location.pathname.match(/^\\/n\\/([a-z0-9-]+)$/);\n  try {\n    if (m) {\n      const r = await fetch(`/v1/notes/${m[1]}`);\n      if (!r.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${r.status}`);\n      const note = await r.json();\n      document.title = `${note.title} · Field notes`;\n      app.innerHTML = `<article><h1>${esc(note.title)}</h1><p class=\"meta\">${esc(note.date)}</p>${note.html}</article>`;\n    } else {\n      const r = await fetch(\"/v1/notes?limit=50\");\n      if (!r.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${r.status}`);\n      const notes = await r.json();\n      app.innerHTML = \"<ul>\" + notes.map(n => `<li><a href=\"/n/${n.slug}\">${esc(n.title)}</a></li>`).join(\"\") + \"</ul>\";\n    }\n  } catch (e) {\n    app.innerHTML = `<section class=\"notfound\"><h1>NOT FOUND</h1><p>No note lives at this address.</p><p><a href=\"/\">Back to all notes</a></p></section>`;\n  }\n  function esc(s) { return String(s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g, c => ({\"&\":\"&amp;\",\"<\":\"&lt;\",\">\":\"&gt;\",'\"':\"&quot;\"}[c])); }\n})();\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat README.md NOTES.md'","aggregated_output":"# fieldnotes.example — site + API\n\n- `site/` — the static front end (S3 + CloudFront, same domain). Every page is\n  one HTML shell; `app.js` fetches the content from the API and renders it.\n- `api/` — the API (Lambda behind the same CloudFront distribution, under `/v1/`).\n  `api/routes.md` lists the routes.\n- `search-console/` — exports from Google Search Console, 2026-10-16.\n\nPages are at `/n/<slug>` (CloudFront rewrites `/n/*` to `/index.html`).\nSitemap lists all 58 note pages.\nIndexed pages in Search Console: 25 on Sep 1, 21 on Oct 16, while I published\nnine new notes in between. Every note opens fine in Chrome, Safari and curl\n(HTTP 200, full content). Nothing in the app changed since August except\nrobots.txt and the new notes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat search-console/url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt search-console/pages-2026-10-16.csv'","aggregated_output":"URL: https://fieldnotes.example/n/drip-line-pressure\nLive test, 2026-10-16\n\nAvailability: URL is available to Google\nCrawl: allowed (robots.txt)\nIndexing: Page cannot be indexed: Soft 404\nPage fetch: Successful (HTTP 200)\nRendered page title: \"Field notes\"\nRendered page text (excerpt): \"NOT FOUND  No note lives at this address.  Back to all notes\"\nURL,Last crawled,Verdict,Reason\nhttps://fieldnotes.example/,2026-10-15,Indexed,\nhttps://fieldnotes.example/n/first-frost-dates,2026-08-29,Indexed,\nhttps://fieldnotes.example/n/mulch-depth-trial,2026-08-31,Indexed,\nhttps://fieldnotes.example/n/drip-line-pressure,2026-10-12,Not indexed,Soft 404\nhttps://fieldnotes.example/n/compost-thermometer-week-3,2026-10-13,Not indexed,Soft 404\nhttps://fieldnotes.example/n/soil-ph-kit-review,2026-10-14,Not indexed,Soft 404\nhttps://fieldnotes.example/n/rain-barrel-overflow,2026-10-10,Not indexed,Soft 404\nhttps://fieldnotes.example/n/bean-trellis-v2,,Not indexed,Discovered - currently not indexed\nhttps://fieldnotes.example/n/greenhouse-vent-timer,,Not indexed,Discovered - currently not indexed\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat site/robots.txt site/sitemap.xml api/routes.md'","aggregated_output":"User-agent: *\nDisallow: /v1/\nDisallow: /admin/\n\nSitemap: https://fieldnotes.example/sitemap.xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<urlset xmlns=\"http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9\">\n  <url><loc>https://fieldnotes.example/</loc></url>\n  <url><loc>https://fieldnotes.example/n/soil-ph-kit-review</loc><lastmod>2026-10-11</lastmod></url>\n  <url><loc>https://fieldnotes.example/n/compost-thermometer-week-3</loc><lastmod>2026-10-09</lastmod></url>\n  <url><loc>https://fieldnotes.example/n/drip-line-pressure</loc><lastmod>2026-09-30</lastmod></url>\n  <url><loc>https://fieldnotes.example/n/first-frost-dates</loc><lastmod>2026-08-20</lastmod></url>\n  <!-- 53 more -->\n</urlset>\n# API routes (all under /v1/, same domain as the site)\n\n| Method | Path | Auth | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GET | /v1/notes | none | list public notes (`?limit=`) |\n| GET | /v1/notes/{slug} | none | one public note (JSON with `html`) |\n| POST | /v1/notes | bearer | create a note |\n| PUT | /v1/notes/{slug} | bearer | edit a note |\n| POST | /v1/notes/{slug}/reactions | bearer | react (per user) |\n| GET | /v1/me | bearer | the signed-in user |\n| GET | /v1/me/drafts | bearer | the user's drafts |\n| POST | /v1/auth/token | none | sign-in exchange |\n\nUnauthenticated POST/PUT return 401. Crawlers hitting POST-only paths with GET\nwere logging 404s and 405s all September, which is why `/v1/` was added to\nrobots.txt on 2026-09-07.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"Search Console’s rendered view shows “NOT FOUND” even though the page fetch returned HTTP 200. The note content comes from `/v1/notes/<slug>`, and `robots.txt` currently blocks all of `/v1/`. I’m narrowing that rule to the private API paths and adjusting the UI so an API failure does not claim the note is missing."}}
