nd network failure rendering.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"The note URLs return HTTP 200, but their content is loaded from `/v1/notes/<slug>`. `robots.txt` blocked that API path, so Google’s rendered page showed “NOT FOUND”—the text recorded in Search Console—and was classified as a Soft 404.\n\nI updated [robots.txt](/tmp/h-1kHB1H/site/robots.txt) to allow public note requests and [app.js](/tmp/h-1kHB1H/site/app.js) to show “NOT FOUND” only for an actual API 404. The cause, fix, and remaining limitation for genuinely missing slugs are in [ANSWER.md](/tmp/h-1kHB1H/ANSWER.md).\n\nLocal checks passed for live notes, missing notes, and API or network failures. Nothing was deployed or sent to an external service."}}
